explanation:
`Series K` is `HahnSeries.Nonpositive ℝ K`: the subring of `K⟦ℝ⟧` made of series whose support lies in (-∞, 0]. The definition builds `coefficientOne`, the Hahn series on ℕ whose coefficients are all 1. It then pushes this series forward with `embDomain` along the order embedding n ↦ -(1/(n+1)). The result has coefficient 1 at each exponent -1/(n+1) and coefficient 0 everywhere else, which is exactly Σ t^{-1/(n+1)}. The proof obligation only checks that these exponents are nonpositive.

The lemmas that follow in the file match the intended object:
- the support is exactly the range of the embedding;
- the support has order type ω;
- the supremum of the support is 0 and is not attained;
- the coefficient at 0 is 0.

This is a specific object, so it is not too narrow merely for being specific. The setting (a coefficient field K, exponents in ℝ) is the one used in Berarducci's paper and in the rest of the library.
